* CABSRT15 - CONTROL FILE CONSOLIDATION FOR THE BALANCING REPORT
* THE CONTROL FILE IS WRITTEN WITH DISP MOD, SO EVERY ATTEMPT AT
* EVERY PROCESS IS ON IT INCLUDING THE ONES THAT WERE RERUN.
* THIS SORT PUTS THE FILE IN PROCESS AND STEP ORDER SO THAT THE
* E35 EXIT SEES EVERY ATTEMPT AT ONE PROCESS TOGETHER AND KEEPS
* ONE OF THEM.  THE ORDER MATTERS BECAUSE THE EXIT HOLDS ONLY ONE
* RECORD AT A TIME AND WORKS ON THE KEY BREAK.
*
* THIS SORT TAKES SORT, RECORD, MODS AND END AND NOTHING ELSE.
* THE EQUALS SETTING THE DFSORT CARD CARRIED IS GONE, SO INPUT
* ORDER WITHIN EQUAL KEYS IS NOT PRESERVED HERE.  KEEPING THE
* LAST ATTEMPT IS NOW DECIDED INSIDE E35 EXIT CABSXLST FROM THE
* RERUN NUMBER AND THE CYCLE DATE ON THE TWO RECORDS INSTEAD OF
* FROM THE ORDER THEY LEAVE THE MERGE.
* THAT RULE IS NO LONGER VISIBLE ON THIS CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(13,8,CH,A,21,3,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(180)
 MODS E35=(CABSXLST,2048,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
